WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.314
Welcome to OurWater.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:07.378
In this video you will learn what the Tool
marketplace is, how to open a tool,

00:00:07.498 --> 00:00:09.754
and how to ask for a new one.

00:00:09.874 --> 00:00:13.138
You will also see what a Tool Admin can do.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:17.502
The Tool marketplace is in the Advanced view
of the menu.

00:00:17.622 --> 00:00:22.494
Right now the switch at the top left says
Easy, so the marketplace is hidden.

00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:25.189
Press Advanced.

00:00:25.309 --> 00:00:27.925
More choices appear in the menu.

00:00:28.045 --> 00:00:31.069
Look for Tool marketplace, and press it.

00:00:31.883 --> 00:00:34.187
This is the Tool marketplace.

00:00:34.307 --> 00:00:38.003
A tool is a small helper that does one job
with your data.

00:00:38.123 --> 00:00:40.883
You only see the tools given to you.

00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:44.309
Tools sit on shelves by subject.

00:00:44.429 --> 00:00:46.997
Here is the Check dam calculator.

00:00:47.117 --> 00:00:52.037
Its card says what it does: how much water a
check dam put into the ground.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:55.346
To use a tool, press Open.

00:00:55.466 --> 00:00:57.938
There is nothing to set up first.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.582
The tool opens on a page of its own.

00:01:01.702 --> 00:01:05.014
We will not use it now, so let us go back.

00:01:05.817 --> 00:01:08.433
Is the tool you need not on the shelf?

00:01:08.553 --> 00:01:11.001
Anyone can ask for a new one.

00:01:11.121 --> 00:01:14.145
Press Request a tool, at the top right.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.822
A form opens.

00:01:16.942 --> 00:01:20.086
Say what the tool should do and who it is for.

00:01:20.206 --> 00:01:23.758
An OurWater administrator reads every request.

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:26.455
Give the tool a name.

00:01:26.575 --> 00:01:28.615
Keep it short and clear.

00:01:28.735 --> 00:01:30.895
I type Rainfall summary.

00:01:31.717 --> 00:01:35.077
Then say what it does, in your own words.

00:01:35.197 --> 00:01:37.933
One or two sentences are enough.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:42.326
Pick a category, so the tool goes on the right
shelf.

00:01:42.446 --> 00:01:44.918
I choose Rainfall and climate.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.974
The last box is optional: who the tool is for,
and why.

00:01:50.094 --> 00:01:53.478
It helps the administrator understand what you
need.

00:01:54.283 --> 00:01:56.155
Press Send request.

00:01:56.275 --> 00:01:58.891
A message says the request was sent.

00:01:59.717 --> 00:02:05.741
Your request now waits under Your requests,
with its name, what it does, and your note.

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:11.518
The label reads Waiting for a Super Admin, an
OurWater administrator.

00:02:11.638 --> 00:02:16.582
If the answer is yes, the tool joins the shelf
and you become its Tool Admin.

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:20.182
If it is no, the reason appears on this card.

00:02:20.983 --> 00:02:23.383
Changed your mind while it waits?

00:02:23.503 --> 00:02:26.575
Press Withdraw request, and it is gone.

00:02:26.695 --> 00:02:31.519
You can ask again any time, with up to three
requests waiting at once.

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:34.222
Now the other side.

00:02:34.342 --> 00:02:38.350
I am signed in as the Tool Admin of the Check
dam calculator,

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:41.902
which is who you become when a request is
approved.

00:02:42.022 --> 00:02:46.006
The card has an extra label: You are its Tool
Admin.

00:02:46.817 --> 00:02:51.137
Next to Open is a Manage button, and a count
of the people added.

00:02:51.257 --> 00:02:53.129
Press Manage.

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:56.086
Manage opens a panel.

00:02:56.206 --> 00:03:00.910
First comes the list of people who can use
this tool, each one by name.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.262
The Tool Admin has a label.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.987
Remove takes a person's access away.

00:03:07.107 --> 00:03:10.467
The Tool Admin's own row has no Remove button.

00:03:10.587 --> 00:03:14.739
Only an OurWater administrator can make
another Tool Admin.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:20.326
To give someone the tool, type their email
under Add people by email.

00:03:20.446 --> 00:03:24.502
You can type several, with a comma or a new
line between them.

00:03:25.317 --> 00:03:27.189
Press Add.

00:03:27.309 --> 00:03:29.637
This note shows what happened.

00:03:29.757 --> 00:03:31.797
Both addresses were added.

00:03:31.917 --> 00:03:37.893
The second person is not on OurWater yet, so the
tool is ready when they sign up with that email.

00:03:38.717 --> 00:03:42.365
Both people are now in the list, and the count
says four.

00:03:42.485 --> 00:03:45.749
The new address is marked Not on OurWater yet.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:48.518
Below is Details.

00:03:48.638 --> 00:03:53.438
A Tool Admin can change the tool's name and
description here, and its Link,

00:03:53.558 --> 00:03:56.222
which is where the Open button goes.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:59.330
That is the Tool marketplace.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:05.906
Open the tools you were given, ask for one that is
missing, and as a Tool Admin, choose who may use it.

00:04:06.717 --> 00:04:08.997
That is the Tool marketplace.

00:04:09.117 --> 00:04:11.781
Thanks for helping look after our water.
